  "task": {
    "name": "Story gate and CI merge-check gate disagree: single-interpreter dev gate greenlights changes the CI matrix rejects",
    "slug": "issue-1945",
    "story_path": null,
    "story_text": "## Observed behavior\n\nA story passes its dev-phase gate and is marked complete, then its pull request is blocked because the required merge checks fail. The gate the story runs to prove itself exercises a single interpreter on the dev/orchestrator host; the checks that govern landing run a multi-version matrix. A change that is green on the single local interpreter but breaks another matrix version is greenlit by the story gate and only caught after the PR is opened, surfaced as a landing failure rather than a gate failure.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nThe gate a story must pass to be considered shippable must exercise the same environment surface that the required merge checks enforce. A commit that the merge's required checks will reject must not be reported as passing the story gate. The gate that clears a story and the gate that governs its landing must not disagree about whether the same commit is shippable \u2014 otherwise \"complete\" is not a truthful status and the disagreement is discovered only as a post-hoc merge failure.\n\n## Diagnosis\n\n- **Observed symptom:** #1934 passed its local dev gate (reported DONE), but PR #1943's CI gate failed on Python 3.11/3.12/3.13 with 8 failures in the workspace/venv code the story changed; the story was reported complete while the merge sat blocked.\n- **Ruled out:** the #1944 process-supervision entanglement (these CI failures are deterministic \u2014 the same 8 tests, fast, on every run \u2014 not the variable nested-fails/standalone-passes signature) and a merge conflict (the PR was MERGEABLE).\n- **Confirmed cause:** the story gate runs a single interpreter (the orchestrator/dev host's Python), while landing is governed by required checks running a 3.11/3.12/3.13 matrix. The two gates cover different environment surfaces, so a matrix-breaking change passes the story gate and fails the landing gate.\n- **Affected code path:** the gate command/definition used in the dev phase versus the CI workflow's required checks, and the interpreter/environment matrix each covers.\n- **Fix-success criterion:** a commit that the required merge checks will fail is not reported as passing the story gate \u2014 the story gate exercises, or is validated against, the same matrix the merge enforces.\n",
    "github_issue": 1945,
    "fix_ready": false,
    "readiness_warnings": [
      "bug Diagnosis section missing required component: evidence"
    ]
  },
